# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 91 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-21, build 4205f93; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 49.0 s to 5487.1 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 91 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-21, build 4205f93; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 49.0 s to 5487.1 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 40
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.5
field_pull_wraps 65
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the second stream of 2026-10-21, from a relay launch of its own, 91 minutes
# cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured as the first (Windows.Graphics.Capture, the mouse
# pointer in the picture, the small-change frames left out, the pool on a device of its own) and
# the first stream with a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine: 327017 of
# its 329945 presents were copied there, 2928 drawn, none failed. Much of it is dialog and
# cutscenes (about 30 of its 91 minutes move). The policy is the one the tree ships. The game
# hitched (20 to 100 ms) 203 times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more 41 times an hour, in 93
# bursts, 41 of them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released 7 times (5 an
# hour), each 0.15 to 0.45 s after a burst of hitches or inside one: at 2636.9, 2664.2, 2940.5,
# 3053.5, 3054.2, 3381.0 and 4937.9 s. The worst blend run, 40 presents from 3053.5 s, is the
# fourth release, inside a burst of 8 hitches and a 184 ms stall. Of the 52 moves on the replay, 5
# land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 49.023 s, from the 2495
# marked frames in its first 41 s, all on time and within 0.40 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 5438.1 s with no holes, opens on gameplay in a dark room and ends on gameplay after the
# sleep wheel, so the cut is the whole video, 49.0 s to 5487.1 s of log time, and the marked
# frames lie inside it. Every second inside the cut that falls out of the 60 fps regime is a
# hitch second, 21 of them in 19 runs, none longer than 2 s, so nothing was removed from the
# middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.5% against 0.5% (0.5% and worst run 40 on the dejitter arm, which is how
# the stream ran), worst run 40 against 40, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 63 against 65. Counted over this window, blends are 1636 against 1621, repeats 462
# against 462, skips 140 against 140, and lock releases 8 against 7: the seven of the field at the
# same moments, and one more on the replay at 1519.3 s with no hitch in the 3 s before, where the
# field's lock held. The replay makes 52 moves, 15 of them late, and the field's log has 53 in the
# window. The 15 blends, 2 pull wraps, 1 release and 1 move by which the two differ were not
# traced present by present.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 40
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.9
min_reseeds 77
max_pull_wraps 63
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 650502
